3861
04:13:25,590 --> 04:13:32,670
Obviously... Well, not obviously for everyone, I guess, but for me, Band of Brothers is definitely up there amongst one of the best.

3862
04:13:32,810 --> 04:13:33,730
And it's only one season.

3863
04:13:34,270 --> 04:13:35,250
It's a mini-show.

3864
04:13:35,530 --> 04:13:36,610
Or a mini-series.

3865
04:13:38,310 --> 04:13:41,410
Then we have... Let me think.

3866
04:13:42,370 --> 04:13:45,230
Probably The Wire is up there.

3867
04:13:45,350 --> 04:13:46,490
You know, The Bunk.

3868
04:13:47,170 --> 04:13:47,890
All that.

3869
04:13:51,740 --> 04:13:53,140
What else is really good?

3870
04:13:53,320 --> 04:13:55,080
I'm trying to think of something very different.

3871
04:13:56,780 --> 04:13:58,940
I mean, I like a bunch, you know, Game of Thrones.

3872
04:13:58,940 --> 04:14:00,900
I like Westworld Season 1.

3873
04:14:01,360 --> 04:14:03,620
True Detective Season 1 was absolutely stellar.

3874
04:14:05,500 --> 04:14:07,140
I mean, I guess I'm very vanilla.

3875
04:14:07,460 --> 04:14:11,920
I like what most people like, because there's a reason most people like it, because it's good, right?

3876
04:14:12,300 --> 04:14:12,980
I don't know.

3877
04:14:16,470 --> 04:14:17,330
Twin Peaks?

3878
04:14:17,790 --> 04:14:20,090
I wouldn't say it's my absolute favorite of all time.

3879
04:14:20,870 --> 04:14:21,690
Definitely not.

3880
04:14:22,130 --> 04:14:24,810
But I would say Season 3 of Twin Peaks was Peek.

3881
04:14:27,350 --> 04:14:28,810
In fact, it's Twin Peek.

3882
04:14:32,420 --> 04:14:34,700
Season two of Twin Peaks was horrible.

3883
04:14:34,980 --> 04:14:35,500
I hated that.

3884
04:14:35,960 --> 04:14:37,340
Well, the second part of it.

3885
04:14:37,800 --> 04:14:40,240
First part was good, because there was still Lynch.

3886
04:14:42,120 --> 04:14:43,440
And it actually was good.

3887
04:14:44,720 --> 04:14:48,720
Better Call Saul is fantastic, and Breaking Bad... Yeah, yeah, yeah, those two are masterworks.

3888
04:14:48,980 --> 04:14:59,340
By the way, I don't know if you heard this, people, but Vince Gilligan, the creator of Breaking Bad and Better Call Saul, is working on his next series now.

3889
04:14:59,790 --> 04:15:01,530
And it's apparently science fiction.

3890
04:15:02,450 --> 04:15:03,650
How about that, huh?

3891
04:15:04,230 --> 04:15:06,290
When I read that, I got so pumped.

3892
04:15:07,510 --> 04:15:08,490
Holy shit.

3893
04:15:10,170 --> 04:15:10,650
Right?

3894
04:15:13,070 --> 04:15:15,650
Like, it's gonna be amazing because it's Vince Gilligan.

3895
04:15:15,750 --> 04:15:16,650
You know it's gonna be good.

3896
04:15:18,710 --> 04:15:20,030
And I love sci-fi.

3897
04:15:22,190 --> 04:15:23,590
I can't wait for that.

3898
04:15:24,370 --> 04:15:26,550
I have no idea what it's gonna be or anything.

3899
04:15:27,800 --> 04:15:30,380
Don't even remember where I read that, but I read it somewhere.

3900
04:15:31,260 --> 04:15:33,160
Mr. Robot was fantastic, yes.

3901
04:15:34,080 --> 04:15:34,700
Blizz Girl.

3902
04:15:34,900 --> 04:15:37,120
I have a distinct memory from Mr. Robot.

3903
04:15:37,300 --> 04:15:38,480
I was watching it with my friend.

3904
04:15:40,480 --> 04:15:42,420
And... I forgot which season it was.

3905
04:15:42,540 --> 04:15:43,340
One of the later ones.

3906
04:15:43,760 --> 04:15:47,860
But there was one episode, and all I'm gonna say is that episode was shot in one take.

3907
04:15:48,020 --> 04:15:49,200
Or at least it seemed to be.

3908
04:15:49,600 --> 04:15:49,940
Right?

3909
04:15:50,500 --> 04:15:52,340
And there was a sequence at the beginning.

3910
04:15:52,860 --> 04:15:54,380
Before the title drop...

3911
04:15:55,020 --> 04:16:00,680
And it was so epic that when the title dropped, we both looked at each other and went, HOLY SHIT!

3912
04:16:03,540 --> 04:16:06,180
I remember that distinctly.

3913
04:16:06,340 --> 04:16:07,360
It was so good.

3914
04:16:08,560 --> 04:16:12,320
We both had, like, movie boners at that moment, you know?

3915
04:16:16,500 --> 04:16:19,580
How do you feel about the western and space genre of sci-fi stuff?

3916
04:16:20,640 --> 04:16:22,580
I did not enjoy Mandalorian very much.

3917
04:16:22,720 --> 04:16:24,020
I did enjoy Firefly a lot.

3918
04:16:24,160 --> 04:16:25,780
That was a fantastic series.

3919
04:16:27,340 --> 04:16:28,200
Unfortunately cancelled.

3920
04:16:32,490 --> 04:16:34,830
I don't know about Project Hail Mary, Space Lover.

3921
04:16:34,890 --> 04:16:35,210
What is that?

3922
04:16:36,550 --> 04:16:38,390
Never seen or heard of Cowboy Bebop.

3923
04:16:40,130 --> 04:16:40,790
That's not true.

3924
04:16:40,870 --> 04:16:41,490
I have heard of it.

3925
04:16:41,690 --> 04:16:43,710
I've heard the name before, but I never knew what it was.

3926
04:16:45,990 --> 04:16:48,010
Westworld Season 1 is fantastic.

3927
04:16:50,250 --> 04:16:57,990
I'm convinced to this day they made Westworld Season 1 just so Anthony Hopkins can do his thing and do his monologues.

3928
04:17:00,030 --> 04:17:01,430
Westworld is his world, you know?

3929
04:17:01,670 --> 04:17:03,590
Everyone is living in his world.

3930
04:17:05,230 --> 04:17:06,090
It's so good.

3931
04:17:07,330 --> 04:17:08,930
Would you like to know what a chunk is?

3932
04:17:10,630 --> 04:17:11,310
Yeah, sure.

3933
04:17:11,930 --> 04:17:15,270
I mean, I assume it's just a patch of land in Minecraft.

3934
04:17:15,830 --> 04:17:24,130
Since everything is in squares, I'm assuming it's just a huge square of maybe, I don't know, X by X amount of blocks, right?

3935
04:17:27,750 --> 04:17:30,130
Oh, yeah, okay, so I figured.

3936
04:17:30,290 --> 04:17:31,710
16 by 16, okay, yeah.

3937
04:17:32,390 --> 04:17:32,790
Thanks.

3938
04:17:34,150 --> 04:17:40,390
I figured it was something like that, you know, and if it's... I think I had it on 20 chunks, the simulation distance.

3939
04:17:41,710 --> 04:17:50,990
So I had an approximate idea of how large a chunk would be, you know, because when I was out exploring early on, none of my shit at home had updated, right?

3940
04:17:51,170 --> 04:17:56,010
So I knew I had to be outside of 20 chunks already, so it couldn't have been too big.

3941
04:17:57,140 --> 04:17:58,180
Yeah.

3942
04:18:01,920 --> 04:18:03,560
Single favorite science fiction story?

3943
04:18:03,840 --> 04:18:05,020
Oh, oof.

3944
04:18:05,980 --> 04:18:06,600
Fucking hell.

3945
04:18:06,820 --> 04:18:08,580
You're asking me hard questions here.

3946
04:18:09,060 --> 04:18:10,120
I can't choose.

3947
04:18:10,360 --> 04:18:11,440
It's simply too difficult.

3948
04:18:12,960 --> 04:18:24,340
But off the top of my head, and there could be others that rate higher in my mind that I just can't think of right now, but Contact by Carl Sagan is probably very much up there.

3949
04:18:27,340 --> 04:18:27,820
And...

3950
04:18:27,850 --> 04:18:31,470
That is one of the few examples where the movie is actually better than the book.

3951
04:18:31,910 --> 04:18:36,510
Not that the book was bad, but the movie is phenomenal.

3952
04:18:38,810 --> 04:18:39,450
Love it.

3953
04:18:42,990 --> 04:18:44,270
I have seen Dune.

3954
04:18:45,150 --> 04:18:46,030
It was okay.

3955
04:18:46,390 --> 04:18:48,410
It's not my favorite, for sure.

3956
